      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KIMCHI (5) continued his good form when he drew wider and went back last start but worked home in good style to finish just a head from the winner in second at Ballarat. Came from the back row to score at this circuit and distance prior. Big chance. TASTE IT (7) put the writing on the wall with back-to-back placings then drew on the back row but made up plenty of ground for a narrow win at this circuit and distance last week. May need a bit of luck negotiating a very wide starting position but with even luck she is capable of another big performance. OUR MYSTERY BET (1) comes back in grade and should enjoy the favours from this draw so can turn things around. HOME AND DRY NZ (2) gets his best draw since he placed from this barrier four back at Ballarat so is worth considering.",
